TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R5","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – Orbit Specifics","issue":"A geostationary orbit is at about 35,786 km and must be equatorial; 600 km is LEO. A GEO cannot remain fixed over the Great Barrier Reef (roughly 10–24°S)."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"Ocean acidification is stated as leading to coral bleaching. Bleaching is primarily driven by thermal stress, so the causal claim is incorrect or oversimplified."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress – Editing & Finalisation","issue":"Text says weeks 7 and 8 are for review and finalisation, but the Gantt chart schedules Editing & Finalisation in weeks 9–10."}],"overall":"Good mission motivation and a usable Gantt chart, but the orbit choice is technically wrong (GEO at 600 km cannot hover over the reef), the plan has no contingencies or explicit sources, and preliminary technical results are minimal. Presentation is adequate with some inconsistencies.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":24.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"The concept, rationale and need (bleaching monitoring, near-real-time relay, SST, thermal stress, bathymetry) are clear and supported by footnoted sources. However, mission objectives and quantitative requirements (revisit, resolution, latency) are not specified, and users are essentially limited to scientists. Referencing is URL footnotes rather than a full reference list, and the acidification causal claim is loose.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Hundreds of millions of humans rely on reefs for food, natural protection, jobs, and tourism."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":5.0,"scale":10.0,"points":15.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"A detailed weekly Gantt chart with deadlines and task descriptions makes the plan feasible-looking. However, no contingencies or variations are provided, information sources are only vaguely named, and the plan's text contradicts the chart on editing weeks. The orbit choice is technically unsound, which undermines confidence in the plan's grounding in the mission concept.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Weeks 7 and 8 are reserved for review, amendments, final simulations, and reflection."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"My current choice is a geostationary orbit at an altitude of 600 km"}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Some work is evidenced (literature review, STK tutorials), but no technical results, calculations, orbit analysis or STK outputs are presented. The progress is minor and not interpreted, so it falls short of showing the design is on track.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4"},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"I have read the brief of Asner’s monitoring system in Hawaii"}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":12.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Clear headings, consistent superscript footnotes and a readable Gantt chart are positives. Weaknesses include awkward phrasing, the chart is not formally captioned as a figure, the text and chart conflict on editing weeks, and references are URL footnotes rather than a reference list.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Oceans have become 30 percent more acidic since the industrial revolution"},{"where":"Image 1","quote":""},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Detailed task descriptions can be found on the next page."}]}]}
